<title>BURUNDI: African leaders agree to keep sanctions on Burundi.</title>
<headline>African leaders agree to keep sanctions on Burundi.</headline>
<dateline>BUJUMBURA 1996-10-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>African leaders agreed on Saturday to maintain their economic embargo against war-torn Burundi despite a suggestion from the United States that sanctions should be eased.</p>
<p>&quot;The summit reiterated that the objective of the sanctions is to serve as an effective means of securing a negotiated settlement between all parties to the conflict,&quot; they said in a statement.</p>
</text>
